  <h1>Who I Am</h1>

  <p>
    I’ve always been drawn to understanding things more deeply — not just what happened, but why it happened, what shaped it, and what it means after.
  </p>

  <p>
    A lot of my life has been spent around systems and technology, but I don’t see them as separate from people. The way something is built, the way it fails, and the way it is experienced all say something about the world behind it.
  </p>

  <p>
    I value clarity, sincerity, and thoughtfulness. I like work that has structure, but I also like space for feeling, memory, and reflection.
  </p>

  <p>
    This portfolio is not just about what I do. It’s also about how I think, what I notice, and the kind of person I’m still becoming.
  </p>
